Report readback with reused offsets (on top of KZ3 patch 2027). 2027 writes a ZPASS report twice: at walk time the
offset's last real count, a frame later this query's count. ToD reuses report offsets for different objects, so the
walk-time value can be another (hidden) object's 0, and an older readback can land over a newer GET_REPORT at the same
offset: wrong zeros the game culls by -- the character flicker (Ratchet missing, his shadow drawn; gone with
LD_OQ_READBACK=0 in tods-play-1137, back in 1140). Now the walk-time value is "visible" (0xFFFF, cellGcmSys's answer
without a count) and a readback reaches the guest only if it is the newest walked GET_REPORT for its offset
(rsx_oq_rb.h). LD_OQ_RB_BASE=1 restores 2027's behaviour. Log: "[report-readback] 7017 on: superseded=N walk-pending=N"
next to 2027's line. Host test: R&C port/rc/tests/run_oq_readback_test.sh (base: 39 of 80 reads give Ratchet 0; now 0).

